-- title:
--   Odd cyclic subgroups determined by the Vélu quotient's j
-- statement:
--   Work over the field $K = \mathrm{HahnSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of Hahn series with rational exponents and coefficients in an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $K$ whose discriminant is a unit (`W.IsElliptic`), and assume its $j$-invariant $j(W)$ is transcendental over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $n$ be a natural number and let $Q, Q'$ be points of the associated affine curve $W$ each of additive order exactly $2n+1$. For a point $P$ write $\mathrm{coordsOrZero}(P)$ for its pair of affine coordinates, with the point at infinity sent to $(0,0)$, and let $S_Q = \{\mathrm{coordsOrZero}(kQ) : 1 \le k \le n\} \subseteq K \times K$, and similarly $S_{Q'}$; the Vélu quotient $\mathrm{veluQuotient}\ S$ is the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $W$ and with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5\sum_{P \in S} t(P)$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2\sum_{P \in S} t(P) - 7\sum_{P \in S} w(P)$. Assume the discriminants of the two Vélu quotients $\mathrm{veluQuotient}\ S_Q$ and $\mathrm{veluQuotient}\ S_{Q'}$ are nonzero — so that both are elliptic and have a $j$-invariant — and that these two $j$-invariants are equal. Then the cyclic subgroups generated by $Q$ and by $Q'$ coincide: $\mathbb{Z}Q = \mathbb{Z}Q'$ inside the group of points of $W$.
--
--   This is the injectivity of $C \mapsto j(E/C)$ on cyclic subgroups of a fixed odd order $N = 2n+1$, for a curve whose $j$-invariant is transcendental over $\mathbb{Q}$ (so that the curve has no extra endomorphisms). It is used in the study of the modular polynomial $\Phi_N$ over the Hahn series field: the fibre-polynomial factorisation into Vélu quotient $j$-invariants, the root-membership criterion for odd level, and the construction of elliptic points with prescribed cyclic subgroup orbits.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_zmultiples_eq_of_veluQuotient_j_eq_of_transcendental.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X0
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_Velu
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_OddOrderSummingSet

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open WeierstrassCurve WeierstrassCurve.Affine

theorem WeierstrassCurve.zmultiples_eq_of_veluQuotient_j_eq_of_transcendental
    [DecidableEq (HahnSeries ℚ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))]
    (W : WeierstrassCurve (HahnSeries ℚ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))) [W.IsElliptic]
    (ht : Transcendental ℚ W.j) (n : ℕ) (Q Q' : W.toAffine.Point)
    (hQ : addOrderOf Q = 2 * n + 1) (hQ' : addOrderOf Q' = 2 * n + 1)
    (hΔ : (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q n)).Δ ≠ 0)
    (hΔ' : (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q' n)).Δ ≠ 0)
    (hj : haveI : (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q n)).IsElliptic := ⟨isUnit_iff_ne_zero.mpr hΔ⟩
      haveI : (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q' n)).IsElliptic := ⟨isUnit_iff_ne_zero.mpr hΔ'⟩
      (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q n)).j = (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q' n)).j) :
    AddSubgroup.zmultiples Q = AddSubgroup.zmultiples Q' := by sorry
